# Tuveloz app — local environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored; never commit real values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# IMPORTANT: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is embedded in the compiled JavaScript
# bundle and is readable by anyone who installs the app. Only publishable,
# client-safe identifiers belong here.
#
#   - Firebase web config keys are publishable by design; access is controlled
#     by Firebase Security Rules and Supabase RLS, not by hiding these.
#   - The Supabase *anon* key is publishable. The service-role key is NOT —
#     it must never appear in this file or anywhere in the app.
#
# Anything genuinely secret (Stripe secret key, service-role key, webhook
# signing secrets) belongs to a server, not to the app. See
# docs/decisions/0004-firebase-auth-with-supabase-rls.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Authentication (Project settings → Your apps → Web app config)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Project settings → API)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
